{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116138",
      "title": "Avoiding Zone Pollution",
      "lectureOrder": 198,
      "videoOrder": 190,
      "sourceHash": "3313c74c1acc00e6142129881bc779f376ab856bea834d08bbdd9270f2eb633f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.37,
          "en": "Another optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "you might want to keep in mind when writing Angular code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 10.08,
          "en": "is that you should consider telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.08,
          "end": 15.08,
          "en": "if a certain event does not matter for change detection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.18,
          "end": 17.16,
          "en": "And here's an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.16,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "In this CounterComponent I'll implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 24.543,
          "en": "the OnInit interface, which is imported from Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 30.99,
          "en": "This, as you learned, forces me to add the ngOnInit method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.99,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "And in there I'll now use the setTimeout function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 36.24,
          "en": "that's built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "So that's not Angular-specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 39.993,
          "en": "but instead comes from the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.16,
          "end": 44.61,
          "en": "SetTimeout allows me to set a timer, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.61,
          "end": 49.47,
          "en": "to four seconds, by entering that amount in milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.47,
          "end": 51.24,
          "en": "And after this timer expires",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.24,
          "end": 53.043,
          "en": "this function here will execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "In here we could then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 59.193,
          "en": "reset our count to zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.75,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "If I do that, you'll see that if I reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 67.23,
          "en": "and I change the counter after four seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 70.68299999999999,
          "en": "it will reset to zero and change detection will run again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "But now let's say we have a second counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "here in the same component to keep things simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "which runs after five seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 86.72,
          "en": "where I just want to log something, or do something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 90.42,
          "en": "that has no direct impact on the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "and the data we manage in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 97.917,
          "en": "But here I'll just log something and say, \"Timer expired.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "So this is now a timer, which when it expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "technically won't have any influence",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "on any template or any component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 110.613,
          "en": "because I'm not changing any data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you'll see that if you reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "and you wait four seconds the first timer expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 121.14,
          "en": "But if you then wait one extra second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.14,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "this second timer expires, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "and change detection ran again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "And it did run again because, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "your entire application is in that zone.js zone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "which under the hood listens to all kinds of events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "for example, also expired timers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "And it then triggers Angular's change detection mechanism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "Because zone.js does not look into your code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 154.14,
          "en": "and see that this code won't have any effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.14,
          "end": 156.27,
          "en": "on any data or component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 160.35,
          "en": "Instead, zone.js just sees that the timer expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 164.13,
          "en": "and that could potentially mean that something changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.13,
          "end": 166.44,
          "en": "and therefore it tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.44,
          "end": 168.243,
          "en": "to run change detection again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "That's why for situations like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "Angular gives you a tool that allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 179.133,
          "en": "to opt out of change detection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 184.92,
          "en": "or to opt out of the zone.js watch mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.92,
          "end": 187.593,
          "en": "for this code here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 192.33,
          "en": "And to use this feature, you have to inject something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.33,
          "end": 196.29,
          "en": "into the component where you want to opt out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.29,
          "end": 197.94,
          "en": "You have to inject a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.94,
          "end": 201.03,
          "en": "which I'll store in a property called zone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "though the name does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 205.41,
          "en": "And I'll inject with the inject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.41,
          "end": 208.773,
          "en": "but you could also use the constructor of course, as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 212.94299999999998,
          "en": "And the injection token here is NgZone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 216.81,
          "en": "And that's provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216.81,
          "end": 219.06,
          "en": "And that's in the end, a class token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 221.88,
          "en": "It's a class I'm injecting here, like a service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.88,
          "end": 225.24,
          "en": "And it is, in the end, a service that gives me a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "that allows us to opt out of zone.js watch mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 231.903,
          "en": "for some specific code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.89,
          "end": 235.41,
          "en": "So here in the place where I have this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.41,
          "end": 238.5,
          "en": "I can now use this zone property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 242.403,
          "en": "and call the runOutsideAngular method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 246.72,
          "en": "And to this method you have to pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.72,
          "end": 250.05,
          "en": "which then wraps the code that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.05,
          "end": 254.46,
          "en": "outside of Angular's change detection, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.46,
          "end": 257.403,
          "en": "Or outside of the zone.js watch mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 258.51,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "And with that this code will not be watched by zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.14,
          "en": "and change detection will not be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.14,
          "end": 267.303,
          "en": "when this timer expires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 273.29,
          "en": "And that is an optimization you will probably not need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 277.35,
          "en": "too often, but sometimes it could be important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.35,
          "end": 280.23,
          "en": "and it could be helpful because it can help you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.23,
          "end": 284.4,
          "en": "avoid unnecessary change detection cycles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 284.4,
          "end": 288.57,
          "en": "So here in this case, if I reload and we then wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.57,
          "end": 291.36,
          "en": "after four seconds, the first timer expires,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.36,
          "end": 293.73,
          "en": "and then after one second, the second timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 293.73,
          "end": 297.09000000000003,
          "en": "And as you can see, I now only get that timer log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 297.09000000000003,
          "end": 299.94,
          "en": "but not the log from all these components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 299.94,
          "end": 303.99,
          "en": "because now indeed, change detection wasn't triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 303.99,
          "end": 306.78,
          "en": "This is, by the way, a concept that's also known",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 306.78,
          "end": 311.43,
          "en": "as avoiding zone pollution because you're not polluting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.43,
          "end": 316.053,
          "en": "zone.js with events that don't matter in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
